Requested per CARRYOVER.md section A item 5, to re-verify the earlier claim that
OneShotDelegation had already been unregistered. It had not — a second instance existed,
holding a live Domain Admin credential, contradicting CARRYOVER's own "DONE" note.

Background: the earlier CARRYOVER note ("Unregister OneShotDelegation — DONE, next session")
referred to the FIRST instance of this task, created and stalled before the ShouldProcess/
ConfirmImpact fix was diagnosed. That first instance genuinely was unregistered. To retry
delegation once -Confirm:$false was added, the task was re-registered ("re-ran via the same
scheduled-task mechanism," per delegation-complete.json) — necessarily the same way, with a
stored -User/-Password principal, since that's how the mechanism works. That second instance
was never cleaned up after its successful run. This is exactly the gap CARRYOVER's own claim of
completeness didn't catch.

